  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Economic empowerment</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Dignity Pasifik (DP) is a women-led local business development services (BDS) provider focusing on improving women&#x2019;s agency and economic empowerment. In addition to strengthening DP&#x2019;s own operational and financial management capacity, Strongim Bisnis provided support in their development of a &#x2018;Rural Women Business Development Manual&#x2019; and supported DP with the initial roll-out of the Manual with trainings of BDS providers located in rural communities in Guadalcanal, Malaita and Honiara. The Ministry of Women, Youth, Children and Family Affairs and DP formed a partnership to expand the BDS training program to savings groups in Central, Choiseul, Western, Malaita, Guadalcanal and Honiara.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tier 2 Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="0" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Food security</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Following temporary Covid-19 travel restrictions, MK Local Food Haus, a woman led fresh vegetable retailer, developed a mobile marketing platform that connected farmers in east Guadalcanal Province with household customers in Honiara. Solomon Islanders residing abroad could also order and pay for fresh vegetables to be delivered to households in Honiara. From an initial handful of suppliers, Strongim Bisnis has supported the Food Haus to expand their network of horticultural produce suppliers to 84 farmer households from 20 communities, with 48 of these households&#x2019; receiving training on poultry and vegetable farming, in addition to financial literacy and business skills.</narrative>
    </description>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-07-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2023-06-30"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
